      "content": "Accepting the loss is a very rational conclusion when the foundation has crumbled. If the structure is a void, then continuing to pour energy into it is not resilience; it's self-sabotage dressed up as hope. It makes perfect sense to recognize when the game is over and to stop the drain. Sometimes, the most honest and logical act is to simply cease the effort, to let the weight lift by letting go of the fight entirely.",
